/**
 * gemini_ocr — single consolidated OCR tool (per API design rule: one tool,
 * not an upload/run/parse triplet).
 *
 * OCR ONLY. This tool NEVER re-runs OCR output through another model to
 * "fix" garbled spans (C2: Haiku/Gemini are unsafe for Hebrew OCR
 * correction). If a page's transcription looks unreliable, the tool reports
 * that via `confidence`/`notes` on the page result — it does not silently
 * rewrite the text. Any correction pass is a downstream, Sonnet-only
 * concern outside this tool's scope.
 *
 * Pipeline:
 *   1. detect_text_layer.py (PyMuPDF) — classify each requested page as
 *      born-digital (text extracted directly, Gemini never sees it) or
 *      scanned (needs vision OCR).
 *   2. Batch math (gemini_ocr_batching.ts) — cap this invocation to
 *      PER_CALL_PAGE_CAP pages total; truncate + report continuation info
 *      if page_range asks for more (Quality Bar #19).
 *   3. For scanned pages: rasterize_pages.py (pdftoppm -r 250) into a fresh
 *      temp dir, then Gemini vision calls STRICTLY SEQUENTIALLY in batches
 *      of GEMINI_BATCH_SIZE pages (C1 — never parallelize; a parallel run
 *      previously corrupted output). Temp dir is removed after each batch,
 *      success or failure.
 *   4. finishReason on every Gemini call is checked and mapped to an
 *      actionable structured error if not STOP (Quality Bar #20).
 *
 * Types/schemas live in gemini_ocr_types.ts; default (subprocess/fs) I/O
 * implementations live in gemini_ocr_deps.ts; pure batch math lives in
 * gemini_ocr_batching.ts. This file is orchestration only.
 */
